{:adr-id "2607152500"
 :title "cloud-itonami Wave 4 rollout start — amendment to ADR-2607121000 P3->P4 gate"
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :author "Jun Kawasaki"
 :status :accepted
 :amends ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan"]
 :context
 "ADR-2607121000 phased Wave 4 (human-services) strictly after Wave 3
  (production-robotics) reached accumulated trust evidence. Live
  wave-maturity-summary computed 2026-07-15 from kotoba.industry.wave /
  kotoba.occupation.wave over current registry.edn: ISIC wave3 66/298
  (22%) implemented, ISCO wave3 26/127 (20%) -- nowhere near a
  completed trust track record. ISCO wave0/wave1 are both 100%
  complete (55/55, 79/79). An earlier 18-agent haiku fan-out batch
  produced a 61% defect rate (empty implementations, missing modules,
  false all-tests-green claims) across cloud-itonami-isic-* actors
  (ADR-2607152300), and kotoba-lang/industry still carries unlanded
  fix/wave3-batch2-quality-audit / fix/wave3-batch-count-drift
  branches from that incident. Owner explicitly directed (2026-07-15,
  via /loop, chose 'supersede ADR first' when asked) starting Wave 4
  now regardless of Wave 3 completion state."
 :decision
 {:scope-of-amendment
  "ADR-2607121000's wave taxonomy, value function and reverse-
   topological ordering rationale are UNCHANGED. Only the P3->P4
   precondition in Section 5 is amended: Wave 4 rollout may now
   proceed IN PARALLEL with Wave 3, not gated on Wave 3 completion.
   Skipping wave 0-2 remains rejected per the original ADR; this
   amendment lifts exactly one precondition (wave3-before-wave4)."
  :quality-guardrails-mandatory
  "haiku-model efficiency is permitted only paired with: (1) no large
   parallel fan-out -- one batch = one-or-few targets, verified-redo
   shape only (cloud-itonami-isic-0510/0520 module shape: advisor/
   governor/phase/operation/store/sim, langgraph-clj StateGraph,
   independent Governor, closed :propose-only op allowlist, phase 0->3
   rollout); (2) agent self-reported 'all tests green' is untrusted
   until independently re-run with real pass/fail counts shown --
   registry :spec->:implemented promotion happens only after that
   independent verification; (3) Wave-4-specific: satellites are
   coordination-only, medical/care-plan/medication/restraint/end-of-
   life/safety-authority-override decisions are permanently excluded
   from the closed op allowlist and any such-adjacent op always
   escalates, never auto-commits."
  :flagship-target
  "ISIC 873 (Residential care activities for the elderly and
   disabled) -- chosen because it is ADR-2607121000's own stated
   largest-long-run-TAM rationale for wave 4 (Japan aged-care
   demographic wedge); currently :spec with :repo nil, fresh scaffold
   from scratch."}
 :consequences
 ["ADR-2607121000's dependency-DAG ordering logic is preserved; only
   the wave3-before-wave4 precondition is lifted, on explicit owner
   authority, with a written record"
  "61%-defect-incident lessons (small batch, verified-redo, distrust
   self-reported green) are carried forward into wave 4 explicitly"
  "this amendment is scoped narrowly -- it is not a general license to
   ignore wave ordering; wave 0-2 gaps (ISIC wave2 at 24%) still follow
   ADR-2607121000 priority"
  "wave 3 work continues in parallel, unaffected by this amendment"]
 :references
